# installer-base-amd64.pkgs — always-on core toolset, AMD64 variant.
#
# Derived from manifests/installer-base.pkgs (Sky1/arm64). Every package
# there is arch-portable EXCEPT the three called out below — see
# docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md for the full accounting. Consume the same way:
# grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)'.

# --- initramfs builder --------------------------------------------------
dracut
dracut-core

# --- DKMS accelerator rebuilds ----------------------------------------------
# gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu DROPPED — that was the arm64 cross-compiler target
# for Mali's gpu.mk invoking aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc explicitly. AMD64 has no
# equivalent CIX accelerator DKMS stack (there is no CIX GPU/NPU/VPU on this
# architecture at all — see docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md "dropped" bucket).
# Native `gcc` below is sufficient for any AMD64-native DKMS module.
dkms
build-essential
gcc
make
flex
bison
bc
libelf-dev
libselinux-dev

# --- disk / partition identify -------------------------------------------
util-linux
parted
gdisk
nvme-cli
smartmontools

# --- hardware identify ---
pciutils
usbutils
dmidecode
lshw

# --- filesystems + recovery ---
btrfs-progs
e2fsprogs
testdisk

# --- boot management ---
efibootmgr
# 2026-09-16 (operator: "standardize on rEFInd on amd64, we should not
# diverge"): grub-efi-amd64 + grub-pc-bin REMOVED. AMD64 now boots rEFInd,
# same as arm64/Sky1 -- see post-install/70-bootloader.sh's
# run_refind_amd64() and assets/refind/ncz-refind-refresh-amd64.sh. The
# rEFInd binary (assets/refind/refind_x64.efi) is a vendored build-time
# repo asset, not an apt-installed package, matching arm64's
# refind_aa64.efi -- extracted from Debian's own `refind` .deb (0.14.2-2.1,
# trixie/sid; not yet in forky) since this project never apt-installs
# `refind` itself on the target.
#
# Known scope reduction, flagged rather than silently dropped: rEFInd is a
# UEFI-only boot manager, so this removes support for real legacy-BIOS-only
# x86 hardware (grub-pc-bin was the BIOS path). Every real AMD64 target
# this project currently builds/tests against (T2 Macs, PROTEUS/CERBERUS/
# HYDRA/ACHILLES) is UEFI, so this is not believed to affect any live
# target -- revisit if a genuine BIOS-only target ever needs support.
#
# rescue-amd64.pkgs' OWN grub-efi-amd64/grub-pc-bios/memtest86+/ms-sys/
# syslinux/syslinux-efi are UNRELATED to this and were NOT touched -- those
# are standalone recovery-USB/BIOS-boot tooling for the rescue environment
# itself, not the main OS's bootloader choice.

# --- network / diag ---
dbus
dbus-broker
iwd
wireguard-tools
network-manager
netplan.io
iproute2
net-tools
iputils-ping
ethtool
tcpdump
mtr-tiny
curl
wget

# bolt (boltd/boltctl) -- userspace Thunderbolt device authorization/
# management. Was entirely absent from this manifest. Metal-confirmed
# missing on MEDUSA (T2 MacBook, real Kensington AD4010T4 Thunderbolt 4
# Dock physically attached): the kernel's own thunderbolt subsystem and
# firmware boot-time authorization already get a real device connected
# and working at full USB4 40Gb/s (confirmed via `boltctl list` showing
# status=authorized, authflags=boot -- BIOS/firmware pre-authorized it
# before bolt.service ever ran), so basic dock functionality (USB
# hub/ethernet passthrough) does not strictly need this package. But
# without it there is no userspace visibility or approval flow for any
# NEW/untrusted Thunderbolt device -- it would connect with no way to
# see, approve, or set a security policy for it. rfkill/PCIe hardware
# itself was never the gap; only this package was missing.
bolt
rsync
firmware-realtek
firmware-linux-free
firmware-linux
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-atheros
firmware-bnx2
firmware-bnx2x

# --- operator quality-of-life ---
htop
tmux
vim
mc
tree
jq
lsof

# --- remote access ---
openssh-server
inetutils-telnetd
openbsd-inetd
busybox-static

# --- zstd (same Debian-vs-Ubuntu gap as the Sky1 manifest documents) ------
zstd

# --- NCZ kernel channels — AMD64 line -------------------------------------
# linux-image-cixmini / cixmini-boot DROPPED — Sky1-only kernel package
# names. AMD64 real package names are TBD pending the two AMD64 kernel
# builds currently in progress (v7.2.6+T2 unified stable on PROTEUS, v7.3-rc3
# edge on CERBERUS) actually landing as packaged .debs — see
# docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md. Placeholder names, confirm against the real
# built package names once available:
#   linux-image-amd64-ncz-t2      (stable, unified T2+regular)
#   linux-image-amd64-ncz-edge    (edge)

# --- locales ---------------------------------------------------------------
locales

# --- console font ---
console-setup
kbd
